WEBVTT

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:33.030
At the moment, there have been no major changes in the battle situation.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:34.410
Chapter 19

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:34.410
Tears

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.370
When the next set of orders arrive, we'll take action immediately.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.030
Until then, we're going to be on standby here.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.540
It's not confirmed yet,

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.210
but reports say that the Imperial Army is gathering strength slowly.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.540
Before the orders arrive, I would like

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.720
everyone to rest well and save their energy.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.900
That is all.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.000
Yes, sir!

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.300
Susie, let's go to the canteen together.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.310
Okay.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.770
It's painful just looking at those two.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.460
Although they're probably trying to escape from their own feelings by burying themselves in their work,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.810
I wish they'd think about those of us watching from the sidelines.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.910
In the end, the people around them won't be able to help no matter what.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.140
We can only wait for the commander...

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.810
...to solve this problem himself.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.650
The commander's having a tough time, isn't he?

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.550
Let's hope that he'll pull through.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:35.130
That's all for the report.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.370
I see.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.710
Say, Welkin...

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.060
About what happened earlier...

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:41.860
I...

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.740
Sorry, but could you set this matter aside for now?

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:47.320
Welkin.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:48.290
I'm sorry.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:50.700
2nd Lieutenant Gunther!

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.360
What is it?

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.450
Commander Varrot is looking for you.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:54.320
Understood.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.780
Faldio.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.090
Can we talk?

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:05.890
Are you all right?

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.570
What do you mean?

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.170
Something happened between the two of you, right?

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.020
I'm fine.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.880
Compared to what Welkin's going through, this is nothing.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.410
Quite admirable.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.280
Why are you doing all this?

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.870
For someone with no relatives like myself,

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.860
Squad 7 is just like a family.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.010
Plus...

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.440
Please don't start hating my brother.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.400
I made a promise with Isara...

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:37.110
I see.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.420
If it gets tough, you can talk to me anytime.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.050
I'll definitely help you.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:43.980
Thanks.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.600
I'm heading off then.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.240
2nd Lieutenant Gunther reporting.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.230
Sorry to call you when you're so busy.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:55.330
Not at all.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.670
How are things?

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.130
The squad is on standby.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.340
We're waiting on a replacement operator for the Edelweiss.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.580
That's not what I'm asking.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.060
I want to know how you feel.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.310
I'm sorry.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:14.340
I felt like I understood how it feels to lose someone dear to you,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.740
but I don't know what to say at a time like this.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:19.640
Not at all.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.520
The replacement is already here.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.090
He should arrive at Amatoria today.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.210
I called for you...

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.840
...because I wanted to discuss the next operation.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.870
Squad 7's next objective is...

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.340
...Bruhl.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.040
Bruhl...

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.550
I don't think this will be too much of a strain, but...

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:50.020
fighting to reclaim one of our towns that were taken by the enemy should have meaning for you.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.990
Yes, Ma'am. Thank you very much.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.820
The orders to attack Bruhl should come soon.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.070
Before that, familiarize yourself with the plan.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.490
Understood.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.210
And...

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.800
It might be cruel saying this now, but...

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.530
When you're free,

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.740
clean up your sister's personal belongings.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.050
I wanted to see if something in him had changed...

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.010
But it was inevitable.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:25.160
He lost his one and only family member, after all.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.890
I heard the driver for this died.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.380
They should give it to our squad then.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.500
Don't touch the Edelweiss!

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:36.960
What's with you? {I added this in. -Ky}

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.710
That's enough! Get away!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.000
Hey!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.770
Why are you so angry?

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.770
Brother!

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:41.490
Let go!

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:42.940
Hey, cut it out!

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.550
So Alicia, you agree, right?

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.630
Jeez, Alicia. You're not listening, are you?

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.180
No...

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.700
Sorry.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.890
Long time no see.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.080
Yo.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.110
Zaka!

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.140
I see.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.730
That girl's...

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.500
A bunch of things happened after that.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.550
I feel like I'm starting to understand what you said.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.770
A bunch of things, huh?

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:49.430
Well, as long as you live, there will always be a bunch of problems.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.700
The most important thing is how you react to them.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.190
Will you face reality and take it on?

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.900
Or will you keep your back to it?

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.250
You're quite hopeful, aren't you?

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.650
We're in an era like this, after all.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.900
I've witnessed a countless number of my comrades dying.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.290
But it's worrisome, isn't it?

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.680
I'm talking about your squad commander.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.460
Yeah, it is.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:24.310
So, why are you here?

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:26.870
What? You haven't heard?

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.760
My name is Zaka.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.990
I'll be burdening Squad 7 starting today.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.190
Please take care of me.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.830
Isn't this guy...

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.510
...the one from the resistance that one time?

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:41.540
By the way, my role is a driver.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.870
In other words, the Edelweiss is...

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.340
Oh yeah. Where's the commander?

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.140
Something wrong?

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.120
These are Isara's...

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:20.870
Is this all she had?

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.070
It was like this too back then.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.240
When we first met,

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.550
Isara didn't bring much baggage along.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.430
This is Isara. Starting today, she's your sister.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.790
Get along well with her.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:51.440
Hey.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.010
What is it?

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.640
Why do you have so few pieces of luggage?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.890
Well, I don't mean to pry...

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.050
Doesn't it bother you?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.500
What does?

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.700
My hair color...

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.350
...and this cape.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.450
Not at all.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:14.030
But...

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.220
There's no point in asking the obvious.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.250
More importantly,

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.250
we'll be siblings from now on.

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.680
I want to know more about you.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.190
Isn't that normal?

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:31.550
You're a weird person.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:34.150
Yeah, I get that a lot.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.240
The reason why my baggage is so light...

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.340
is because I never stayed in one place for long.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:45.310
Only carrying what's important makes travel more convenient.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:46.400
I see.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.360
You don't have to worry about that anymore, then.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:52.530
We'll always be together from now on.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.760
I'm happy to meet you, Isara.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:03.070
Yes, Brother.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:11.420
Isara...

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:42.040
The Valkyrur have the ability to heal faster than normal humans.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.360
Using Ragnite as a medium,

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.810
they can make use of god-like powers.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:53.580
I wasn't mistaken after all.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.460
Alicia is a Valkyria.

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:04.780
What do I want to do exactly?

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:15.110
Starting now, Squad 7 will begin a new operation.

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:17.860
Our objective is Bruhl.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:21.010
Our first goal is to reclaim the town.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.690
In our squad, there are people who were born in Bruhl.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.050
I'm also one of them.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:27.960
Let's go!

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.500
Strategically, it's not very important.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:38.130
However, Commander Varrot specially arranged this for us. We mustn't disappoint her.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:41.750
We must minimize the damage to the town.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.620
Recover Bruhl as quickly as possible!

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.250
I've finally returned.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.000
Our hometown.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.910
We've returned to Bruhl.

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:06.090
The vow I made then...

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.260
And I'll definitely come back.

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:10.710
Back to this Bruhl where the lion's paws bloom.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.670
I'll fulfill it.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:16.380
Isara.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.650
I'll do it.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.970
In my own way.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:24.140
I'll put an end to what I started.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.350
So watch me.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.280
Squad 7...

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.980
Begin operation!

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:40.070
That's...

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.260
E-Enemy attack!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.400
It has a great sound.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:49.930
The steering wheel feels great, and the pedals are amazing.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:53.920
This is proof that your previous owner maintained you well.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:55.950
I can go on forever. {There's no problem then.}

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:06.810
Fire!

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.150
Damn!

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:50.950
What?!

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.570
Okay.

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:18.170
The building thought to be the enemy's command center has been confirmed.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.900
Now, we'll take over that-

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:21.310
Ah!

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:23.410
That's...

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.940
Come on, don't cry.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.050
Operation... complete.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.110
Good grief.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.340
She's always crying.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.790
It's fine.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:13.490
She reclaimed her hometown with her own hands.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:14.810
But...

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.970
What about the remaining two?

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:19.170
Are you talking about the commander and Alicia?

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.800
Now that you mention it, they're not here.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.320
Where did they go?

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:24.340
It's their home, after all.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.780
There's probably a bunch of things they want to do.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:28.770
A bunch, huh?

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:31.410
Well, there will be, as long as you're alive.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.380
It's only been vacant for half a year, but...

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.850
It'll be ready soon, Brother.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.040
It's delicious!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.870
In the end,

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.080
we're the same.

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:43.230
You were you.

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:44.790
I was I.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.600
We would never walk the same path.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.420
That's what I thought...

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.440
In the end,

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.770
I couldn't protect my family either.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:59.010
Who is it!?

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:02.740
Alicia...

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:03.920
Sorry.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:05.830
I knew you'd be here.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.430
Everyone's worried about you.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.620
I said that, but it's an excuse.

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:16.010
In all honesty, I'm worried about you.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:21.460
Time really flies.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:24.650
Our first meeting...

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:28.310
The Empire invading Bruhl...

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.520
It was in this house...

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:33.240
that I met Isara for the first time, wasn't it?

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.450
Hey, do you remember?

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:42.400
What I said then.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:45.590
"I'll definitely come back."

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:49.400
The reason I joined the militia...

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:52.580
was because I fought here with you and Isara.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.490
Because it's always been my wish.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.100
I thought that I'd be happier...

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.350
But now...

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.540
Welkin, I...

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:04.740
It's strange.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:07.950
Since Isara left,

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:10.880
I've felt like I've lost a part of my very being.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.600
No, it's not a feeling.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.740
I did lose a part of myself.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.720
Sorrow...

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:19.620
Pain...

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:23.000
I'm always thinking about what happened to Isara.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.090
If I had done something else back then,

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:26.880
and kept her by my side,

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.500
she wouldn't have died!

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.670
I know...

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:33.280
I know how you feel.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.440
What do you know?!

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.020
I know...

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.800
because I've always been at your side!

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.410
Tell me then.

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:45.700
It's been so tough...

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.650
It's been so painful...

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.440
Ever since Isara left,

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.450
I've been in so much pain.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.240
But tears won't come out.

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:12.330
You poor thing.

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:16.330
At times like these,

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.010
you don't have to hold back.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.190
I'll head back first.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.140
Alicia.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.410
You were waiting for me?

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.830
Hey, Welkin. Look.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:33.730
These are...

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:35.860
Lions Paws...

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:12.820
I'm Ramal Valt.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:17.550
Of course, I joined the militia because I wanted to protect Gallia from the Empire!

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.130
But...

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:22.090
I want to become an adult soon,

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:24.110
and become taller and stronger!

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:27.650
That way, I'll be able to protect others properly the next time.

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:31.030
Next on Valkyria Chronicles,

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:33.760
Chapter 20: Beloved One

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:35.770
Among the smell of machine oil,

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:41.000
Chapter 20

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:41.000
Beloved One

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:37.750
sweetness does exist.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.290
I won't forget that.
